============================================================================================
   [PASS] D0  the two routes' alpha_2 is alpha_1/2 - (alp-2bet)(alp+bet+3lam)/((alp-2)(bet+lam)) -- the standard khronometric shape
   [PASS] D1  alpha_1 is REGULAR at the candidate's locus bet = lam = 0 and equals -4 alp there   so alpha_1 has NO pole to hide behind: off the locus it is simply -4 alp
   [PASS] D2  alpha_2 carries a 1/c_123 = 1/(bet+lam) POLE and the candidate sits EXACTLY ON it   at alp = 1/5:  lim_{lam->0} alpha_2|_{bet=0} = oo
   [PASS] D3  alpha_2 carries a SECOND pole at alp = 2 -- and deep MOND needs alp_kh = 2(1-mu) -> 2   lim_{alp->2} alpha_2 = -oo;  the MOND regime is the other singular locus, and the edge of the aether stability domain 0 <= c14 < 2
   along literature bet = lam = -d:   alpha_1(d) = 4*(-alp - 2*d)/(d + 1)   ->   -4*alp  as d -> 0
   along literature bet = lam = -d:   alpha_2(d)|_{alp=1/5} -> -oo  as d -> 0
   [PASS] D4  LIMIT along the approach path: alpha_1 -> -4 alp (NOT 0)
   [PASS] D5  LIMIT along the approach path: alpha_2 -> infinite (NOT 0)   alpha_2 -> -oo

   approach table at alp = 1/5, regenerated from the formulas (compare Route B's routeB_limit_2026.out and the refuter's F-table -- both report these same values):
      d         alpha_1             alpha_2                 
      1/2       -16/5               -2/5                    
      1/10      -16/11              -50/99                  
      1/100     -88/101             -6424/4545              
      1/1000    -808/1001           -5135749/450450         
   [PASS] D6  regenerated table matches the two routes' published approach values EXACTLY   alpha_1 = -16/5, -16/11, -88/101, -808/1001;  alpha_2 = -2/5, -50/99, -6424/4545, -5135749/450450

   D7  READING.  The candidate's own locus (bet = lam = 0, forced EXACTLY by the gravity
       sector K_ijK^ij - K^2 + R3 via Gauss-Codazzi) is a POLE of alpha_2, not a zero.
       Route A, Route B and the refuter all instead solved the linear system AT the locus
       and got alpha_1 = alpha_2 = 0.  Both statements are correct: the map is
       DISCONTINUOUS there.  The value AT the singular point is 0; every neighbourhood of
       it contains theories with alpha_1 -> -4 alp and alpha_2 -> infinity.
       A zero obtained as the value of a rank-deficient system at a strong-coupling point
       is not a physical pass -- it is the signature of a missing mode.

